- Summary:: A report reveals that U.S. public school students lost over 11 million instructional days due to out-of-school suspensions in 2015–16. It highlights the negative effects of suspensions, especially on Black, Latinx, and Native American students, and students with disabilities. The report aims to help policymakers understand and address the disparities in school discipline practices.
