## Highlights
- Across all grades, for every 100 students enrolled, there were 23 days of instruction lost due to out-of-school suspensions. However, this holistic view of all students in all grades obscures the reality that in secondary schools, the rate of lost instruction is more than five times higher than the elementary rates: 37 days lost per 100 middle and high school students compared to just 7 days per 100 elementary school students. ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01jaatjjd4fkgqqt6c5w9v8czm))


